**Theorem 19.2 (the complete-service necessary stopping condition).**
A robust pointwise-finite policy for Definition 19.1 implies that $f$
is locally constant on $S$ in its relative sup-norm topology:

$$
\forall x\in S\ \exists\epsilon>0\
 \forall z\in S:\quad
 \|z-x\|_\infty<\epsilon\ \Longrightarrow\ f(z)=f(x).
\tag{19.1}
$$

This allows arbitrary adaptive rational Adds, Reset, growth with its
actual attached Tick, further Ticks, Holds, malformed complete probes,
range and growth refusals, and arbitrary finite precision requests.
In particular exact entrance identity cannot be robustly acquired
pointwise finitely on all of $\mathbb Q^{V_t}$.

Proof. Fix $x$ and a policy tape. At every enabled Read choose its
lower legal reply
$k=\lfloor2^pa(x)\rfloor$, where $a(x)$ is the actual sampled scalar
at that prefix. Both bits are available after every prefix by
Definition 8.1, so this specifies a legal path, not an independent-noise
assumption. Robust pointwise finiteness gives a finite terminating
complete record on this path.

Freeze its finitely many acquired inputs, replies and policy decisions.
Along these fixed inputs the field at each prefix is a continuous
affine function of an alternative entrance $z\in\mathbb R^{V_t}$.
Initially it is $z$; Add is a fixed translation, Tick a fixed linear
map, Reset a constant map, raw growth a fixed zero inclusion followed
in C by the fixed new-tree matrix, and Read/Hold/refusal leave it
unchanged. All matrices may have changed finite dimensions, but the
entrance dimension remains fixed. Geometry, guard outcomes and range
are determined by the same input frames and initial geometry.
The syntax/precision parser also depends only on acquired bits.

For each recorded Read the identical integer $k$ is legal exactly when

$$
2^pa(z)\in[k-1,k+1).
\tag{19.2}
$$

At $z=x$ the lower-report choice has
$k\le2^pa(x)<k+1$, strictly inside the larger open interval
$(k-1,k+1)$. Continuity therefore gives an open entrance neighborhood
in which that same integer remains legal, even if the baseline scaled
value is exactly the integer $k$. Intersect these finitely many open
neighborhoods; if there were no Reads take the whole entrance space.

Every rational $z$ in that neighborhood and $S$ admits exactly this
complete finite record. This statement follows inductively, rather
than presupposing the policy path: equal earlier replies force equal
next requests and local decisions; (19.2) permits the next recorded
Read, with its own legal bit at $z$; other replies are the same fixed
ones. Identical finite integer values have identical complete frames,
End, local acknowledgement and Return. Proper input prefixes, busy
serialization and all input-determined refusal branches agree as well.
There is no extra field-dependent public observation by Definition 19.1.
Thus the same stop and finite output occur. Robust correctness at
every such $z$ forces $f(z)=f(x)$, proving (19.1).

Identity output would require this neighborhood to contain no other
member of $S$. No rational point of the nonzero-dimensional
$\mathbb Q^{V_t}$ is isolated: perturb one coordinate by an arbitrarily
small nonzero rational. Thus identity fails (19.1) there.
The tree always has at least one vertex, including alpha.
Fixing each random tape proves the pathwise randomized statement.
$\square$

The finite-information principle is classical, including
[Schröder, *Admissibly Represented Spaces and QCB-Spaces*,
arXiv:2004.09450v1, Proposition 2.4](https://arxiv.org/html/2004.09450v1)
and the equality argument in
[Finite Start Predictive Memory, Theorem 8.4](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_FINITE_START_PREDICTIVE_MEMORY.md).
The source-specific obligation here is (19.2) along the entire adaptive
C service. The proof does not assert continuity of deterministic floor
at its integer walls. The two legal outputs provide the open slack.
The existing
[finite-prefix theorem](../../../D5/S3/Observer/SymbolicStability/FinitePrefixLocalConstancy.lean)
and its [Scribe](../../../Blueprint/D5/S3/Observer/SymbolicStability/FinitePrefixLocalConstancy.scribe.cs)
combine given off-boundary neighborhoods; they do not establish this
C report/affine-prefix correspondence.

